cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this bench in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Agent Double Execution Bench"
abstract: >-
  One network fault: what does an agent framework do twice? Seven agent
  frameworks were pointed at a local fake model server that fails on purpose (429, 500,
  dropped connections, silence), and the server's own log records how many requests each
  one sends and how many times a side-effecting tool runs. Default settings everywhere.
  No real API and no cost; anyone can rerun it.
authors:
